Lower the fixed per-call cost of DeepGEMM's FP8/FP4 SiTU Mega MoE kernel
(sm100_fp8_fp4_mega_moe_situ) for decode-sized launches. Applied by
cmake/external_projects/deepgemm.cmake to the pinned DeepGEMM checkout.

- Compact dispatch (<= 64 experts per rank, <= 32 ranks): count atomics only
  for experts that received tokens; receive totals are summed locally after
  the barrier instead of with remote atomics.
- Pre-pull barrier spread over SMs: SM r sends rank r its counts and the
  barrier signal, and every CTA waits on the local signal (no single-SM loop
  and no grid sync after the barrier).
- Combine for decode-sized launches (<= 2 items per warp): one warp per
  (token, 512-byte chunk) loads all selected slots before adding, in the same
  order and with the same rounding; larger launches keep the TMA path.
- Evict-first L2 hint on routed weight loads for decode-sized launches
  (num_tokens * top-k <= BLOCK_M * experts per rank).
- Decode-shaped scheduler order (existing template flag): all L1 tasks before
  L2 when BLOCK_M <= 64 and the ring is not reused.

Outputs are bitwise identical to the unmodified kernel.

